          }
        },
        "b2": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "q": "What makes UraGuard® different from other adult incontinence products?",
            "a": "<p>UraGuard® is designed with women’s health in mind. Unlike standard incontinence products, UraGuard® features patent-pending technology—a discreet shield that helps reduce exposure to bacteria trapped within the product. By acting as a barrier between bacteria and the urethral area, UraGuard® adds an extra layer of protection where it matters most.</p>",
            "open": true
          }
        },
        "b3": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "q": "Is this a pad or a liner?",
            "a": "<p>Neither. Pads and liners absorb. UraGuard® separates your skin from the wet core of the brief you already wear.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "b4": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "q": "How does UraGuard® work?",
            "a": "<p>UraGuard® is a specialized barrier designed to help shield the wearer from bacteria held in the incontinence product. By helping reduce bacterial exposure, UraGuard® supports better daily hygiene and comfort.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "b5": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "q": "Does UraGuard® reduce my exposure to bacteria?",
            "a": "<p><strong>UraGuard® is designed to help reduce your exposure to bacteria inside incontinence products.</strong> Our patent-pending UraGuard® technology acts as a physical barrier placed beneath the urethra, helping reduce bacterial contact with the urethral area. This added layer of protection works within your standard incontinence product to support a cleaner, more comfortable environment.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "b6": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "q": "Who is UraGuard® designed for?",
            "a": "<p>UraGuard® is designed for adult women who experience incontinence and are looking for a product that prioritizes comfort, dryness, and urinary health.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "b7": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "q": "Does UraGuard® work for men?",
            "a": "<p>UraGuard® is specifically designed for women, as it is shaped to fit the female anatomy. Men can continue to use their usual incontinence products, though the UraGuard® shield may not provide the same benefits. We are actively developing a version tailored for men—stay tuned!</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "b8": {
          "type": "group",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Wearing it"
          }
        },
        "b9": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "q": "Which brands does it work with?",
            "a": "<p>All of them: tab-style briefs, pull-on underwear and adult diapers in every size, including Depend®, TENA®, Always Discreet®, Prevail® and store brands.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "b10": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "q": "Will it reduce how much my brief absorbs?",
            "a": "<p>No. UraGuard® is a thin barrier, not an extra absorbent layer. Moisture passes through into your brief as normal; the difference is what stays against your skin.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "b11": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "q": "Is UraGuard® gentle on sensitive skin?",
            "a": "<p>Yes! UraGuard® products are made with soft, skin-friendly materials chosen with sensitive skin in mind. If you experience any irritation, discontinue use and speak with your healthcare provider.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "b12": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "q": "Will anyone be able to see it?",
            "a": "<p>No. It sits inside the brief and adds no bulk. Customers tell us they can’t feel it.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "b13": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "q": "Will it shift or bunch up?",
            "a": "<p>It’s thin, flexible and shaped to fit, with an adhesive back that keeps it in place day or night.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "b14": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "q": "How often should I change my incontinence product?",
            "a": "<p>For optimal comfort and hygiene, we recommend changing your incontinence product as soon as it becomes wet, or at least every 4-6 hours, depending on individual needs. Use a fresh UraGuard® shield every time you change your brief.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "b15": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "q": "Is UraGuard® available as a pull-up or tabbed diaper?",
            "a": "<p>Currently, UraGuard® is available as a shield insert, allowing you to add our barrier protection to any existing incontinence product. However, we understand the need for an all-in-one solution, and we are actively exploring pull-up and tabbed-style options. Stay tuned for updates!</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "b16": {
          "type": "group",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Ordering"
          }
        },
        "b17": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "q": "Where can I purchase UraGuard®?",
